{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791073241,"nonce":"rfJzQquTIQXROabsZZfqU0y2QmY=","title":"CSS animations started again each time they ended","message":"Animations.ended dropped a finished run, then had the cascade restyle the element; the restyle found the animation entry with no run for it and started it again, so a finite animation looped for as long as its rule matched. Seen as a dialog's opening animation replaying. The pixel test's 'ended, back to its own width' passed only because of the restart: the bar has no width of its own, and the restarted animation drew it 10 wide.\n\nFix: a finished run stays on the element's list, holding nothing, so the same entry keeps it; it goes when the entry does. The pixel test gives the bar its own width and checks it stays.","files":null}]}